/* ---------- image prompts ---------- */
const STYLE = `Style: sketched by hand onto an old rolled parchment scroll. Sepia and iron-gall ink linework with charcoal shading, red-ochre and yellow-ochre pigment like Lascaux cave paintings, Egyptian hieroglyphic register lines and small glyph borders, plus a few bold flat shapes of lapis blue in the manner of modern paper cut-outs. Visible parchment grain, uneven hand-drawn lines, soft torn irregular edges that fade into the parchment. No frame, no rectangular border, no sharp corners, no lettering. Wide horizontal composition, 3:2.`;
const PROMPTS = [
 ['One like a son of man (1:12–16)',`A tall figure in a long robe reaching to the feet with a gold sash across the chest; hair white as wool; eyes like flames; feet glowing like bronze in a furnace; face shining like the sun; a sharp two-edged sword coming from his mouth; seven stars held in his right hand; seven separate gold oil lampstands standing around him; the apostle John fallen at his feet on a rocky island shore.`],
 ['The seven churches map (2–3)',`An illustrated map of western Asia Minor (modern western Turkey) and the Aegean coast, with the island of Patmos offshore; seven small walled cities marked along a looping road in this order: Ephesus, Smyrna, Pergamum, Thyatira, Sardis, Philadelphia, Laodicea; a small lampstand drawn beside each city; hot springs drawn at Hierapolis and a cold spring at Colossae near Laodicea; a dashed red route line; a ship sailing from Patmos to Ephesus.`],
 ['The throne room (4:2–8)',`A throne with a rainbow like an emerald around it; flashes of lightning; seven burning torches; a sea of glass like crystal before the throne; twenty-four elders in white with gold crowns on twenty-four thrones in a circle, some casting their crowns down; four living creatures around the throne: one like a lion, one like an ox, one with a human face, one like a flying eagle, each with six wings and covered with eyes.`],
 ['The Lamb who was slaughtered (5:6)',`A small lamb standing upright yet bearing the wound of a sacrifice; seven horns and seven eyes on its head; it stands in the center of the throne scene taking a rolled scroll sealed with seven wax seals; elders bow holding harps and gold bowls of incense.`],
 ['The four horsemen (6:1–8)',`Four horses in procession: a white horse whose rider holds a bow and wears a crown; a fiery red horse whose rider holds a large sword; a black horse whose rider holds a pair of balance scales; a pale gray-green horse, the color of a corpse, ridden by Death, with a shadowy figure of the Grave (Hades) following behind.`],
 ['The countless crowd (7:9–10)',`On one side, twelve tally-mark groups and twelve tribal banners for the 144,000 of Israel; on the other, a huge crowd beyond counting from every nation, in white robes, waving palm branches before a throne and a lamb.`],
 ['Locusts from the abyss (9:1–11)',`Smoke rising from a deep pit; locusts shaped like horses prepared for battle, wearing gold crowns, with human faces, long hair like women's hair, teeth like lions', chests like iron breastplates, rushing wings, and scorpion tails with stingers; a dark angelic king above them named the Destroyer.`],
 ['The mighty angel and the little scroll (10:1–2)',`A huge angel wrapped in a cloud with a rainbow over his head, his face like the sun, his legs like pillars of fire; his right foot on the sea and his left foot on the land; a small open scroll in his hand; seven thunders as dark shapes in the sky; John beside him eating the little scroll.`],
 ['The two witnesses (11:3–12)',`Two prophets in rough sackcloth standing between two olive trees and two lampstands; fire coming from their mouths; a dry sky with no rain; later the same two rising to their feet and ascending in a cloud while a city trembles in an earthquake.`],
 ['The woman and the dragon (12:1–6)',`A woman clothed with the sun, the moon under her feet, a crown of twelve stars on her head; facing her, a huge red dragon with seven heads, each head wearing a royal diadem, and ten horns in total; its tail sweeping a third of the stars from the sky; a newborn child being caught up toward a throne; the woman fleeing into a wilderness on eagle's wings.`],
 ['The beast from the sea (13:1–3)',`A beast rising from churning waves, its body like a leopard with spots, feet like a bear's, mouths like a lion's; seven heads and ten horns in total, with a royal crown on each of the ten horns; insulting names written on the heads as unreadable marks; one head scarred by a healed mortal wound; a red dragon standing on the shore handing it a throne.`],
 ['The beast from the earth (13:11–15)',`A beast climbing out of cracked ground, with two small horns like a lamb's but a dragon's mouth breathing smoke; it calls fire down from the sky; behind it a large statue of the sea beast that crowds bow to; people stamped with a mark on the right hand or forehead.`],
 ['Seven bowls and three frogs (16)',`Seven angels in white with gold sashes pouring seven gold bowls onto land, sea, rivers, the sun and a dark throne; a dried-up Euphrates riverbed; three frog-like unclean spirits coming from the mouths of a dragon, a beast and a false prophet; a low earthen mound, Tel Megiddo, on a wide plain in the distance.`],
 ['The woman on the scarlet beast (17:3–6)',`A woman dressed in purple and scarlet, decked in gold, jewels and pearls, holding a gold cup; she rides a scarlet beast with seven heads and ten horns, covered with insulting names; behind her seven hills and many waters; merchant ships and mourning sailors in the distance.`],
 ['The rider on the white horse (19:11–16)',`Heaven opened; a rider on a white horse with eyes like flames and many crowns on his head; a robe dipped in blood with the words King of kings and Lord of lords written as faint unreadable marks on his robe and thigh; a sharp sword from his mouth; the armies of heaven following on white horses, dressed in white linen, carrying no weapons.`],
 ['Binding the dragon; the thrones (20:1–4, 11)',`An angel coming down from heaven holding a key and a great chain, binding a red dragon and sealing it in a dark pit; above, a row of thrones with people seated on them; in the far distance, a great white throne before which earth and sky flee away.`],
 ['The New Jerusalem (21:10–22:2)',`A radiant city coming down out of heaven, shaped as a perfect cube, shining like jasper and clear crystal; a high wall with twelve gates, each gate a single pearl, with an angel standing at each open gate; twelve foundation stones in different gem colors; a street of clear gold; a river of the water of life flowing from a throne down the middle; the tree of life growing on both banks with twelve kinds of fruit and healing leaves; no sun, the city lit from within.`]
];

